# WHAT SHIPS TO A USER, decided here rather than remembered.
#
# The 2026-08-05 package shipped this extension's own TypeScript source, its
# test suite, its .vscode/ directory, its tsconfig and both logos -- because no
# .vscodeignore existed, and vsce's fallback is .gitignore, which was written to
# answer a completely different question. "Remember to exclude the tests" is not
# a control. This file is.
#
# NOTE the deliberate difference from .gitignore: that file excludes `daemon/`,
# because a 19 MB build artifact does not belong in git history. This file must
# NOT exclude it -- daemon/ is the runtime (daemon + embedder helper +
# models.json) and is the whole point of the package. The two files disagree on
# purpose, and this paragraph is why.
#
# Verified by scripts/verify-vsix.js, which asserts on the ARCHIVE CONTENTS.
# `vsce package` exiting 0 is exactly what produced the broken package.

# --- source, kept out; only compiled output ships ---
src/**
tsconfig.json
**/*.ts
**/*.map

# --- tests, and the 3 GB of VS Code builds their harness downloads ---
out/test/**
.vscode-test/**
.vscode/**

# --- development-only metadata ---
.gitignore
.vscodeignore
package-lock.json
node_modules/**

# --- our own build/verify tooling: runs BEFORE packaging, never inside it ---
scripts/**

# --- previously built packages, so a rebuild never nests one inside another ---
*.vsix

# --- CREDENTIALS. Nothing that could hold a secret, ever. ---
#
# ADDED 2026-09-02 after this was CONFIRMED BY EXECUTION: a .env dropped in this
# directory is listed by `vsce ls`, i.e. it ships to every marketplace user, and
# scripts/verify-vsix.js does not catch it -- all twelve of its patterns are
# filename hygiene (source, maps, tests, node_modules) and none of them is about
# a secret.
#
# THE TRAP IS AT THE TOP OF THIS FILE. The header explains that vsce's fallback
# is .gitignore. That is true only while this file does NOT exist. It exists, so
# .gitignore no longer applies to packaging AT ALL -- and .gitignore is exactly
# where `.env` was excluded. Creating this file to fix one leak silently
# disabled the rule protecting against a worse one.
#
# proxy/.env holds SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, the BYPASSRLS credential. A
# developer putting a .env here for local daemon config is an ordinary thing to
# do, and it is one `npm run package` away from publishing it.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
**/credentials.json
**/service-account*.json

# --- unused assets ---
# logo.jpg has no reference anywhere in src/ or media/main.js: logo.png is the
# webview logo and icon.png is the marketplace tile. It was 147 KB of the last
# package for nothing.
media/logo.jpg
